Use the new Sphinx stylesheet API in the users guide theme.

Sphinx 7.2 turned the entries of css_files into _CascadingStyleSheet objects.
The vendored rtd-theme passes one straight to pathto() in the branch without a
rel attribute, where older Sphinx received a string, so rendering the first
page fails with:

  TypeError: argument of type '_CascadingStyleSheet' is not a container or
  iterable

Upstream fixed this line for 9.12.4 and it remains fixed on master; the 9.14
branch point predates the fix and 9.10 never carried it. The hunk is upstream's
own, taken verbatim from ghc-9.12.4-release:
https://github.com/ghc/ghc/blob/ghc-9.12.4-release/docs/users_guide/rtd-theme/layout.html

Not needed on debian-13, whose Sphinx 8.1.3 still tolerates the old form.
Applies unchanged to 9.10.3 and 9.14.1, whose theme files are byte-identical.

--- a/docs/users_guide/rtd-theme/layout.html
+++ b/docs/users_guide/rtd-theme/layout.html
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
     {%- if css|attr("rel") %}
       <link rel="{{ css.rel }}" href="{{ pathto(css.filename, 1) }}" type="text/css"{% if css.title is not none %} title="{{ css.title }}"{% endif %} />
     {%- else %}
-      <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pathto(css, 1) }}" type="text/css" />
+      <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ pathto(css.filename, 1) }}" type="text/css" />
     {%- endif %}
   {%- endfor %}
 
